      <trans-unit id="help.compare_budget.under">
        <source>help.compare_budget.under</source>
        <target>You drove less than the budget allowed.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_budget.reference">
        <source>help.compare_budget.reference</source>
        <target>Your budget is the distance per day that brings you exactly to your allowance at the end of the lease. Polaris uses it as it was at the start of the period, recorded every day at midnight.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_budget.percent">
        <source>help.compare_budget.percent</source>
        <target>The percentage gives this gap against the second figure. It is left out while less than 6 hours of the period have passed, because it would swing too much.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.answer">
        <source>help.compare_pace.answer</source>
        <target>Are you driving more or less than usual?</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.actual">
        <source>help.compare_pace.actual</source>
        <target>What you drove</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.expected">
        <source>help.compare_pace.expected</source>
        <target>What your pace predicted</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.over">
        <source>help.compare_pace.over</source>
        <target>You drove more than usual.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.under">
        <source>help.compare_pace.under</source>
        <target>You drove less than usual.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.reference">
        <source>help.compare_pace.reference</source>
        <target>Your usual pace is your average distance per day since the start of the lease, with more weight on the last 30 days. Polaris records it every day at midnight; until it has a record for the first day of a period, the row says “Not enough history”.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_pace.percent">
        <source>help.compare_pace.percent</source>
        <target>The percentage gives this gap against the second figure. It is left out while less than 6 hours of the period have passed, because it would swing too much.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_projected_end.answer">
        <source>help.compare_projected_end.answer</source>
        <target>Is your end of lease looking better or worse?</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_projected_end.actual">
        <source>help.compare_projected_end.actual</source>
        <target>Today’s estimate</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_projected_end.expected">
        <source>help.compare_projected_end.expected</source>
        <target>The estimate at the start of the period</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_projected_end.over">
        <source>help.compare_projected_end.over</source>
        <target>The estimate went up: you are heading for more kilometres.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_projected_end.under">
        <source>help.compare_projected_end.under</source>
        <target>The estimate went down: you are driving less than before.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_projected_end.reference">
        <source>help.compare_projected_end.reference</source>
        <target>Every day, Polaris estimates how far you will have driven by the end of the lease and records it at midnight. Until it has a record for the first day of a period, the row says “Not enough history”.</target>
      </trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="help.compare_projected_end.percent">
        <source>help.compare_projected_end.percent</source>
        <target>The percentage gives this gap against the second figure.</target>
      </trans-unit>
